    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its cases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response (and all owner responses).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived fields like `displayName`, `initials`, `namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber`). This makes the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` carry the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto` that derives the tier:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank)\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise\n\nThis follows the repo's existing idiom \u2014 other derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) are computed the same way in the mapper, while the underlying `namesakeCount` and `email` come from the persisted `Owner` model.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`, covering both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique name + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE).",
